From d7ff2ea785a071216a68da023b8ccf8a38683e5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Certe Kim <18364439+CerteKim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 22:30:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: add the Xiaomi Book S 12.4 (a51)

Describe the board on top of sc8180x.dtsi and sc8180x-pmics.dtsi:

 - display: CSOT PNC357DB1-4 driven by the Himax HX83121A over a single
   DSI0 link with DSC, the PMC8180C LPG as backlight;
 - GPU: the higher DVFS states the Adreno 680 firmware advertises;
 - connectivity: WCN3990 WiFi, WCN3998 Bluetooth with a board BD address
   (the chip has none provisioned), NVMe on PCIe2, microSD on SDHC2;
 - audio: WCD9340 with the WSA881x speakers and the VA/TX macros;
 - the RA9530 magnetic stylus charger on i2c7, its bus at the 400 kHz the
   firmware declares;
 - power and volume keys (volume-down is the PMIC RESIN, volume-up the
   first PMIC's key), lid, RTC, thermal zones, USB-C and the SBU muxes.

The device tree for the "oc" GPU variant is gone: the states it was about
are the vendor ones this machine's firmware uses, and they are the default
now.

The board no longer carries its own refgen fixed regulator or the gpu_mem
label: 7.2's sc8180x.dtsi has the real refgen block (wired into both DSI
links, so CONFIG_REGULATOR_QCOM_REFGEN is required) and an 8 KB gpu_mem
region of its own, so the vendor's 20 KB ZAP carve-out is labelled
gpu_zap_mem instead.
